sentences.t:
Assí es vuestra ventura, grandes son vuestras ganancias;
una piel vermeja morisca e ondrada,
Çid, beso vuestra mano en don que la yo aya.”

sentences.l:
Thus is your fortune, great are your gains;
a fur crimson Moorish and honoured,
Çid, I-kiss your hand as gift that it I may-have.”

sentences.t:
Raquel e Vidas las arcas levavan,
con ellos Martín Antolínez por Burgos entrava.
Con todo recabdo llegan a la posada;

sentences.l:
Raquel and Vidas the chests were-carrying,
with them Martín Antolínez through Burgos was-entering.
With all care they-arrive at the house;

sentences.t:
Quando esto ovo fecho, odredes lo que fablava:
“ya don Raquel e Vidas, en vuestras manos son las arcas;
yo, que esto vos gané, bien mereçía calças.”

sentences.l:
When this he-had done, you-will-hear what he-was-saying:
“O don Raquel and Vidas, in your hands are the chests;
I, who this for-you won, well would-deserve hose.”

sentences.t:
Dámosvos en don a vos treínta marcos;
mereçer no' lo hedes, ca esto es aguisado:
atorgar nos hedes esto que avemos parado.”

sentences.l:
We-give-you as gift to you thirty marks;
to-repay to-us it you-will, for this is fitting:
to-grant to-us you-will this which we-have settled.”

sentences.t:
Mandad coger la tienda e vayamos privado,
en San Pero de Cardeña i nos cante el gallo;
veremos vuestra mugier, menbrada fija dalgo.

sentences.l:
Order to-strike the tent and let-us-go quickly,
in San Pero of Cardeña there to-us may-sing the cock;
we-shall-see your wife, prudent lady of-rank.

sentences.t:
Si vos assí lo fiziéredes e la ventura me f[o]re complida
mando al vuestro altar buenas donas e ricas;
esto [h]e yo en debdo que faga i cantar mill missas.”

sentences.l:
If you thus it should-do and the fortune to-me should-be fulfilled
I-promise to-the your altar good gifts and rich;
this I-have I in debt that I-may-make there to-sing thousand masses.”
